<section class="work-process-area pt-120">
    <div class="container-fluid">

        <div class="row justify-content-center">
            <div class="col-lg-10">
                <div class="work-process-wrapper">
                    <div class="row single-process-step align-items-center">
                        <div class="col-lg-8">
                            <div class="process-content-box wow fadeInLeft">
                                <div class="step-count">
                                    1.
                                </div>
                                <div class="content">
                                    <span class="line"></span>
                                    <h3 class="title">
                                        What should you check when you're buying a cat or kitten?
                                    </h3>
                                    <p class="f-20">
                                        Find out how we can help you with this difficult decision.
                                    </p>
                                    <div class="q-a">
                                        <p class="f-20 my-4">
                                            Kittens are cute, (and they know it), but they shouldn’t be judged on that alone. When you decide to get a cat or kitten, it is a big, but also exciting commitment, and there are lots of things to think about before you get one.
                                            You should do your research and find a responsible breeder where the cats and kittens are properly cared for and looked after. You should always try to visit the breeder in person and see how the cats and kittens are bred and cared for.

                                        </p>
                                        <p class="f-20 my-4">
                                            Cats are great company in the house and a fantastic addition to our lives, but it is important to make sure you have the time and resources to care for them properly now, and in the future. Cat ownership is a huge commitment and one that may last for more than a decade. Kittens, in particular, will need different levels of care and attention as they grow, so if that might not fit in with your life in 3 months' time, then it’s important to think long and hard about your decision.
                                        </p>
                                        <p class="f-20 my-4">
                                            A kitten shouldn’t leave its mother until it is at least twelve weeks old, and a kitten who travels over the border needs to be fifteen weeks old before leaving, so it’s very important that you stay aware of this and check their age as best you can. Ask for details - if you are speaking to a responsible breeder, they will know when and where the kitten was born and will be happy to tell you all about their parents and their behavior.
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-4">
                            <div class="process-img wow fadeInRight">
                                <img class="mb-5" src="~/webassets/images/logo/happy-cat.png" />
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="row single-process-step align-items-center">
                        <div class="col-lg-8">
                            <div class="process-content-box wow fadeInLeft">
                                <div class="step-count">
                                    1.
                                </div>
                                <div class="content">
                                    <span class="line"></span>
                                    <p class="f-20 my-4">
                                        Before you agree to take the kitten, you should ask if the kitten is nervous or has any health issues. Keep an eye out for anything mentioned and any potential problems when you visit to collect your new pet. Kittens should have received worming and flea treatment in addition to their first vaccination at 9 weeks of age, and the second vaccination would be at 12 weeks of age, so you should ask if they have received these treatments, and if so, request a copy of the records be sent to you in advance of collection.
                                        All the vaccinations are written on an animal passport by a veterinarian.
                                    </p>
                                    <p class="f-20 my-4">
                                        If a kitten appears very fearful or stressed when you see them, this could be an indication that it hasn’t been properly socialized and will find it harder to adapt to a home environment, especially if it doesn't grow up with other animals or children.
                                    </p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-4">
                            <div class="process-img wow fadeInRight">
                                <img class="mb-5" src="~/webassets/images/logo/happy-cat.png" />
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</section>
